<h2>A responsible diagnostic tool acceptance checklist</h2><ol><li>Confirm exact scanner SKU, VCI hardware and software package against the vendor's published record.</li><li>Document BMW chassis/model year and specific modules being checked.</li><li>Verify the supported protocol, host environment and firmware update state.</li><li>Perform a stationary, read-only connection using official instructions.</li><li>Save VIN-identification results and list of detected control units.</li><li>Read and preserve fault-code evidence without clearing records.</li><li>Check whether required service or active tests appear only as advertised categories or as verified vehicle-specific capabilities.</li><li>Do not carry out write-capable work until approved procedure, training and safety conditions are established.</li></ol>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Does an all-system scan mean every BMW module is supported?</h3><p>No. A scanner can have broad hardware/software architecture while still lacking the exact vehicle variant, module access, protected function or current software entitlement. Validate each required subsystem by the vendor's vehicle coverage information.</p><h3>Is Autel MK900 the same as MK900-TS?</h3><p>No. Autel's own product comparison distinguishes TPMS capabilities and other options between models. Never transfer a feature from a suffixed model to the base model without confirming it in the actual specifications.</p><h3>Is a newer tablet always better than a BMW-focused handheld?</h3><p>No. Platform age, update model, licensed coverage, technician workflow and the particular vehicle task can matter more than screen size. A shop diagnosing multiple makes has different requirements from one owner registering a BMW battery.</p><h3>Can any scanner update BMW module software?</h3><p>No. Coding, resets, adaptations and ECU programming require distinct capabilities, authorization, hardware and safety measures. Do not infer programming from a scanner displaying an active-test menu.</p><h3>Why are the original comparison sources preserved here?</h3><p>Original specialist articles retain distinct model and function exceptions, licensing details and technical figures. Where consolidation is approved, the full independent source body and diagrams are migrated into the canonical reference rather than discarded; every original conversion requires a preservation ledger and verified redirect.</p></section>